pplication/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"257621d692dabe66a5469c42ac7e4b69dde48e81847b06b36b8cff2fea406555","event_uuid":"b9ead6d0-d6fc-4256-95ef-281a9f740aea","position":{"commit_sha":"709566ece95111a546c89571cab5d9afbba687b2","position":"1788383213639233001-b9ead6d0-d6fc-4256-95ef-281a9f740aea"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"93507f497994d17f789160937c628584f6e3fd03f89036ed4cd484a47efcfbf0","event_uuid":"e467eb3a-505b-460c-90df-c5605081c217","position":{"commit_sha":"ce1d30eb9cf933c8b3a5cfd693f3aca2c29ffcb1","position":"1788383219542768001-e467eb3a-505b-460c-90df-c5605081c217"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317530858706001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2de070d1-aebf-481c-a96f-05230853a68d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"8bd75d39-e941-4642-9f74-f32c456db34c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"566b-6e74-8ae9-4dd8"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F12 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), HIGH, **ALREADY DRIFTED**.\n\n## Problem\n\nTwo masters for one fact — which subcommands the CLI has and what they exit:\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` `ROUTES` — 78 live routes, **zero aliases**\n- `docs/exit-codes.md:117` Subcommand table — 81 hand-maintained rows\n\n`docs/exit-codes.md:5-7` claims the file is \"the single source of truth ... pinned by\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py`, which fails if the codes drift.\" The entire\nassertion touching the file (`:236-243`) is\n`assert \"\\`11\\`\" in text and \"block-but-retryable\" in text.lower()`. Nothing checks the table.\n\n## Measured drift — as the inventory recorded it\n\n**Correction to an earlier revision of this plan.** I briefly recorded four stale rows here.\nThat was wrong: the probes behind it were rewritten by a shell hook that folded all argv into a\nsingle subcommand name, so every multi-token invocation looked non-existent. Re-run against the\nvenv binary directly, `bridge fsck`, `bridge check-access` and `bridge setup` are all REAL — they\nare nested argparse subcommands of the `bridge` route (`rebar bridge --help` lists\n`{preview,run,sync,status,pause,resume,fsck,check-access,setup,projects}`). The inventory's\noriginal reading was correct.\n\nThe drift is exactly two rows, in opposite directions, which is why equal-looking counts hid it:\n\n| side | offender | reality |\n|---|---|---|\n| doc row for a non-command | `review` (`:185`) | removed shim; absent from `ROUTES`, not invocable |\n| live route with no doc row | `bridge-status` | invocable; the hyphenated alias of `bridge status` |\n\nVerified by invoking every one of the 81 documented rows: exactly one, `review`, reports\n`unknown subcommand`.\n\n## Approach — add-census-assertion-to-existing-test\n\nSet-difference the table rows against live `ROUTES` names inside `test_exit_codes.py`, and correct\nthe five discrepancies.\n\nPlain set equality would be WRONG, and that is the substance of this ticket. `ROUTES` holds\nTOP-LEVEL route names; the table documents user-facing INVOCATIONS, which include a route's\nnested subcommands. Equality would fail on `bridge setup` and friends — real, working, correctly\ndocumented commands — which is exactly the concept collapse the epic's AC2 forbids. The invariant\nis two-directional but asymmetric: every live route must be documented under SOME spelling, and\nevery documented row must BEGIN with a live route name.\n\nThis does not collapse a distinct concept (epic AC2): the table's Subcommand column and `ROUTES`\nalready denote the same set — the invocable subcommands — and the table's extra columns (exit\ncodes per command) stay hand-authored and unconstrained.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `test_exit_codes.py` asserts the ASYMMETRIC invariant, comparing real parsed values\n      rather than re-listed literals: every live non-retired `ROUTES` name is documented under\n      some spelling, and every table row BEGINS with a live route name. Plain set equality is\n      explicitly NOT the invariant — it would fail on the real nested subcommands (`bridge setup`,\n      `bridge fsck`, `bridge check-access`). Verified by the test passing after the doc is fixed.\n- [x] AC2: the assertion fails in BOTH directions and names the offenders. Verified by two\n      mutation checks — an extra doc row, and a route removed from the compared set — each RED\n      with the offending name in the message.\n- [x] AC3: the one non-invocable row, `review`, is removed. (An earlier revision of this plan\n      claimed four such rows; that came from probes mangled by a shell hook and was withdrawn —\n      the other three are real nested subcommands.) Verified by invoking every documented row\n      through the venv binary directly and finding none that report `unknown subcommand`.\n- [x] AC4: `bridge-status` gains a row documenting its exit behavior. Verified by AC1's equality.\n- [x] AC5: the false pinning claim at `:5-7` is corrected to describe what the test now actually\n      enforces. Verified by reading it against the assertions.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py -q` — the census assertion and\n  its drift cases (AC1, AC2), green only once the doc is corrected (AC3, AC4).\n- `for c in <every row>; do rebar $c --help; done` — proves no documented row is non-invocable\n  (AC3); the census test encodes this so it does not rely on a manual sweep.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"add the missing bridge-status row, remove the stale review row, and correct the pinning claim to state exactly what the test enforces"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py","reason":"the census assertion (route<->table, both directions) and the duplicate-row check"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"],["relates_to","566b-6e74-8ae9-4dd8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"b9ead6d0-d6fc-4256-95ef-281a9f740aea","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd6b-09c5-8f76-45ad","ticket_type":"bug","title":"docs/exit-codes.md has drifted from ROUTES and advertises a gate it lacks (mirror F12)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3dd3d19e-bdf2-418d-8206-57364d04b048","f7045166-5677-47c2-9188-b65fa95dc374","12bc5ea6-b2fa-4044-9a0c-c90ab4f1b449","722fdbad-83d0-4401-a9f5-78792f23c465","0d4f61fb-c4d4-4231-bb79-f06cc0307669","416c0c74-bc4a-4ac7-8e8f-faa14dffa068","528015ef-5127-46d8-ac8e-0b170519ee8e","8bd75d39-e941-4642-9f74-f32c456db34c","3c6e41fe-02da-46d0-9119-e31a33558f68","20832bf6-56c3-4571-b81f-940b1b1414e8","71484be2-f8f8-4507-ad68-76b2017643b7","b9ead6d0-d6fc-4256-95ef-281a9f740aea","e467eb3a-505b-460c-90df-c5605081c217"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788391763953701001,"uuid":"f6f7a640-16fe-463f-8b21-ed8ca2865759"}